<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ragnit</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ragnit, now the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neman">Neman</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Kaliningrad</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, lies on the south bank of the Neman river. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> built a castle there in 1289 on the site of a Scalovian stronghold, and it became a base for campaigns against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>. The brick castle, rebuilt in the late 14th and early 15th centuries, survives in ruins.</p></div>
